  "summary_en": "Washington State statute (RCW 46.75, enacted 2019) regulating personal delivery devices, small automated sidewalk delivery robots supervised by remote operators. It sets operating requirements, insurance, incident reporting, self-certification with the Department of Licensing, device identification and equipment, cargo restrictions, and infraction liability through a registered agent.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines personal delivery devices: under 120 lbs, max 6 mph, automated driving with remote operator supervision.",
   "Operators must carry at least $100,000 general liability insurance.",
   "Incidents with injury or property damage must be reported to local police within 48 hours.",
   "Annual self-certification to Department of Licensing with $50 fee per device; unique ID markers, brakes, lights required.",
   "Bans transporting hazardous materials and alcohol; infractions go to registered agent and are treated like parking infractions."
  ],
